    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "blogtextliquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>The British summer is a rumour that occasionally comes true. You spend eleven months yearning for it, and then suddenly it arrives in a blaze of 28-degree heat, crowded pub gardens, and spontaneous trips to the coast. It is brief, glorious, and completely chaotic.</p><p>Summer fragrance is unique because warmth is a volume amplifier. Heat lifts scent molecules off your skin faster and carries them further on the breeze while testing their staying power against humidity and sunshine.</p>"
      }
    },
